{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>You will surely wear away, both you and this people.</b> As its Targum has it: ״מלאה תלאי״ — 'the matter is too heavy.' It means: you are not able to bear so heavy a burden, for this is great toil and exhaustion for you and for all those who stand before you, for they would tire in vain and would not be able to draw near to you, everyone to present his case before you." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> נבול תבול — like this fig upon which there are fallen figs, as it is said (Isaiah 34:4): ״כנבול עלה מגפן וכנובלות מתאנה״; ״also you״ — to include Aharon; ״also this people״ — to include the seventy elders."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:45.962129061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}